ummary type="html">The scale of the economic disruption caused by AI has led even conservative politicians to talk about universal basic income. But economists are not convinced, and campaigners think we need to ask deeper questions.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Tens of thousands continue to protest across France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fbd5952158bb213e2f54eddae1db26adc5b7d7cc36b0b20e15de88defe79d6f</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:51:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-15T00:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tens-of-thousands-continue-to-protest-across-france/a-79950503--f335770faa0d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tens-of-thousands-continue-to-protest-across-france/a-79950503?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some 106,000 people marched through French cities for a fifth consecutive weekend of protests, marking the lowest turnout in recent weeks.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Philippines wins first Eurovision Song Contest Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d435ffde3ac84f2046a0b1f85642ada38ad2443a92fb9e363d66df88e2635bdb</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:51:05Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T22:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/philippines-wins-first-eurovision-song-contest-asia/a-79950050--13c562f8bc59.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/philippines-wins-first-eurovision-song-contest-asia/a-79950050?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Eleven countries took part in the competition in Bangkok. Teenage winner Carmelle Collado's winning dance song is a tribute to Filipino women.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>SpaceX carries out first-ever spaceship capture</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82ced7fdc0c37f048360c41609fcd98e4ad1b42872e21e2952b8e15a62613a36</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:51:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spacex-carries-out-first-ever-spaceship-capture/a-79950275--a4ef41f2a49e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spacex-carries-out-first-ever-spaceship-capture/a-79950275?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The successful recovery of SpaceX's Starship marks a breakthrough in founder Elon Musk’s goal of developing a fully reusable rocket system.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Germany's 2027 budget: A record €561 billion and a mountain of debt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:042f5b5730245cdf1895b319463c9738c9b8341ea8a62fb46b616434bd9d6b6c</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:51:11Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-s-2027-budget-a-record-_561-billion-and-a-mountain-of-debt/a-79943216--747b01c10ad0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-s-2027-budget-a-record-€561-billion-and-a-mountain-of-debt/a-79943216?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2027 federal budget proposal has finally been hammered out and is set for a vote in parliament. What are the government's policy priorities in defense, infrastructure, the economy and social spending?</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Nigeria's upcoming election marred by rising AI disinformation</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:73e115da96d191261040ede358e24d0ac0a2822b7f378ed5b8ac5c2e88fdf873</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:51:14Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T21:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897--e1618bd315dd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nigeria-s-upcoming-election-marred-by-rising-ai-disinformation/a-79946897?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Nigeria inches closer to the 2027 polls, the use of artificial intelligence in the electoral process has prompted questions about integrity and institutional readiness. Can Nigerians trust their democratic processes?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Sudan pushes back elections amid violent flare-ups</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:877c10bf318f969dd1798441c9f7398bcb68b3ff4eb9de6803e5dc0fff1e8e68</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:51:17Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T20:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-pushes-back-elections-amid-violent-flare-ups/a-79949622--9cf2f881ff78.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-sudan-pushes-back-elections-amid-violent-flare-ups/a-79949622?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Sudan has been independent from Sudan since 2011, and has not yet held national elections. Since then, the country faces cycles of violence after a civil war led to a tenuous peace deal.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US: Duffy says 'incompetence' or bad tech to blame for flight haltings</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b63b1249fc3905fe152a43f48358c01f73b59233b5329376b1602c7282f45b43</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:51:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T20:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-duffy-says-incompetence-or-bad-tech-to-blame-for-flight-haltings/a-79949977--1dd9eb14fa53.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-duffy-says-incompetence-or-bad-tech-to-blame-for-flight-haltings/a-79949977?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Air carriers in the US canceled some 16,000 flights over the past 24 hours in the biggest such grounding since 9/11. Officials hinted that incompetence or faulty equipment, not malfeasance, is the cause.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: 'Iranian' content farms reach millions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b9e36a8d14ce76e4346af4966de2ee0a25d3f63c693103ac55e6dce94d0849e0</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T20:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-iranian-content-farms-reach-millions/a-79934190--0e43f1d33817.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-iranian-content-farms-reach-millions/a-79934190?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Several social media accounts claiming to represent the Iranian military show signs of being part of so-called content farms. DW Fact Check looks at how they operate and how users can spot them.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Italy slaps Meta with €805mn fine over access to Android photos</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f4c591e30416892206ba9bd674efa3634c629e82a3cdc78eaac0fa656c9eb33</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T18:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/italy-slaps-meta-with-_805mn-fine-over-access-to-android-photos/a-79949032--51e9f2bddd4d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/italy-slaps-meta-with-€805mn-fine-over-access-to-android-photos/a-79949032?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Italian regulators say Meta accessed photos and multimedia content from Italian users via the Facebook application for Android devices. Meta said it would appeal the decision, calling the fine "disproportionate."</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>COP31: Protesters, UN urge swift climate deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:65480349450b49608c30baf2bcc693270987d0b15c0e0318782cc24247c10d97</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T17:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cop31-protesters-un-urge-swift-climate-deal/a-79948501--5f86c2781d9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cop31-protesters-un-urge-swift-climate-deal/a-79948501?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The UN climate chief has warned that "tactical delays" at the COP31 climate talks in Turkey could prevent a deal to slow global warming.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Werner Holzer Prize awarded to Katja Gloger and DW's Jaafar Abdul Karim</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:97d06bd87c4e30e66faeceaf2558d83ec0217aa3eef5e67364360e9f59a0c252</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T15:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/werner-holzer-prize-awarded-to-katja-gloger-and-dw-s-jaafar-abdul-karim/a-79946916--5a434ad9f59c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/werner-holzer-prize-awarded-to-katja-gloger-and-dw-s-jaafar-abdul-karim/a-79946916?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW journalist Jaafar Abdul Karim and Russia correspondent Katja Gloger have been awarded the prestigious Werner Holzer Prize for international journalism.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Zelenskyy says security deal could go to referendum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c7e5f6fdc72c8156d123fbb5ba9b0590194c904d9f4bd61dc3f59b0ceaea206c</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-says-security-deal-could-go-to-referendum/a-79947535--17ea05d7ca0f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-zelenskyy-says-security-deal-could-go-to-referendum/a-79947535?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US has broached the idea of Kyiv giving up the Donbas region in exchange for NATO membership, the Ukrainian president said.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>New facilities in Laos and Cambodia: Is China expanding its military presence in Southeast Asia?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:43fd93b14250424b37045c07cdaf509e91d3e094a5eb6c6142802e04040df73d</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/new-facilities-in-laos-and-cambodia-is-china-expanding-its-military-presence-in-southeast-asia/a-79944798--c731be0f2b99.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/new-facilities-in-laos-and-cambodia-is-china-expanding-its-military-presence-in-southeast-asia/a-79944798?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China has been growing its economic relationships in Southeast Asia. Now new military facilities in Laos and Cambodia are causing smaller countries to worry China's military networks are also expanding.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Solar power production approaches record high</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:63a1a1fd57a847889b3c6680d5b668768d8850e70a26d4ac988e216a90eec1ab</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T11:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-solar-power-production-approaches-record-high/live-79947500--1cc60de113f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-solar-power-production-approaches-record-high/live-79947500?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Solar power output in Germany in 2026 has already surpassed last year's total. Meanwhile, experts say the country is headed for a budget crisis. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Wolf Biermann at 90: The singer who defied East Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a6dc4b8ef65d24d133d1f43867fa82e8cf64f7bf8c0e76f3769e3a50af0846c</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T10:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/wolf-biermann-at-90-the-singer-who-defied-east-germany/a-79915297--17726feda083.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/wolf-biermann-at-90-the-singer-who-defied-east-germany/a-79915297?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">His life is a reflection of contemporary German history, which Biermann has addressed via his songs and sharp wit. Turning 90, he’s as feisty as ever.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary: Millions in hidden cash found in Orban graft probe</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:94f7cc8a14dd1251d783a03fd9b72a287ae16714f0a2203adc475d252dc4f536</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T09:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-millions-in-hidden-cash-found-in-orban-graft-probe/a-79946923--46c1c05194eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-millions-in-hidden-cash-found-in-orban-graft-probe/a-79946923?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investigators discovered bundles of banknotes buried in forests and concealed in buildings. The money was seized during an investigation into a former minister accused of accepting millions in bribes.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US loses measles-elimination status after 26 years, WSJ reports</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d7336d92dc6c5fcc22ff9c13034edb88b76e0970a564cac42ee5eef003fb9cf9</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T09:15:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-loses-measles-elimination-status-after-26-years-wsj-reports/a-79946974--cd585e728f91.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-loses-measles-elimination-status-after-26-years-wsj-reports/a-79946974?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Pan American Health Organization has reportedly stripped the US of its measles-elimination status after 26 years, as the country battles its worst outbreaks in more than three decades.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Microsoft says all services working again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:64b2467ff23b096a17ef5802fb8d3a3879188f6aebe299257643e4809286f4fb</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T09:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/microsoft-says-all-services-working-again/a-79946887--03062deb25b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/microsoft-says-all-services-working-again/a-79946887?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US tech giant Microsoft says it has fixed problems that led to a global outage of its services. The glitch severely disrupted online communications in businesses and governments for more than 24 hours.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Sudan: Misery worsens amid plummeting aid for displaced people</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7a6ad8997566cc2f8e10872f323d006308faf4f8b857bc12bc30df40c2c675bc</id><updated>2026-11-15T06:50:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T08:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/sudan-misery-worsens-amid-plummeting-aid-for-displaced-people/a-79938864--624277167dba.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/sudan-misery-worsens-amid-plummeting-aid-for-displaced-people/a-79938864?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Sudan's humanitarian crisis is exacerbated by cuts in international aid. Almost 34 million people are in need as war and drone strikes are making it difficult to deliver aid to the population.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
